Now HUD upHint update and functions. Add to updateHud:
```
const left = Math.max(0, G.upgradeAt - G.kills);
els.upHint.textContent = '∞ · UPGRADE IN ' + (left || 1);
```
When left=0, upgrade opens immediately; but pending. Show 'UPGRADE READY'. Do:
```
els.upHint.textContent = '∞ · ' + (G.pendingUpgrades>0 || G.state==='upgrade' ? 'UPGRADE READY' : 'UPGRADE IN ' + left);
```
Only update if text differs? DOM text set each frame; cheap enough but let's compare.

Add after wave update.

Then functions openUpgrade/chooseUpgrade after hideOverlay.

HTML card markup generation. Use data-index and add listeners; easier: create with innerHTML and assign onclick via index stored in array.

```
function openUpgrade(){
 if(G.state!=='playing' && G.state!=='upgrade') return;
 G.state='upgrade';
 const pool=UPGRADES.filter(u=>(G.up.stacks[u.id]||0)<u.max);
 const copy=pool.slice();
 const choices=[];
 while(choices.length<3 && copy.length){ choices.push(copy.splice((Math.random()*copy.length)|0,1)[0]); }
 G.upgradeChoices=choices;
 els.upgradeCards.innerHTML = choices.map((u,i)=>{
   const st=G.up.stacks[u.id]||0;
   return `<button class="upgrade-card" type="button" data-index="${i}" style="--c:${u.color}">
     <span class="u-key">${i+1}</span>
     <span class="u-icon">${u.icon}</span>
     <span class="u-body"><span class="u-name">${u.name}</span><span class="u-desc">${u.desc}</span><span class="u-level">${st>0?'LV '+st:'NEW'}</span></span>
   </button>`;
 }).join('');
 [...els.upgradeCards.querySelectorAll('.upgrade-card')].forEach(btn=>{
   btn.addEventListener('click',()=>chooseUpgrade(G.upgradeChoices[Number(btn.dataset.index)]));
 });
 showScreen('upgradeScreen');
 tone(520,1040,0.25,'triangle',0.03);
}
```
Note `.u-body` spans display block? CSS .u-name/.u-desc/.u-level are spans but CSS `display` not set → inline. Need `display:block` on these. Add CSS: `.u-name,.u-desc,.u-level{display:block}`. Also u-body flex column makes spans flex items (fine, they become blocks).

`chooseUpgrade`:
```
function chooseUpgrade(u){
 if(G.state!=='upgrade'||!u) return;
 u.apply();
 G.up.stacks[u.id]=(G.up.stacks[u.id]||0)+1;
